{"questions":[{"question_id":"czSLorwmhSeJucEt","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","year":2004,"examDate":2004,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"periodic-table-and-periodicity","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"electronegativity","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"the-formation-of-the-oxide-ion-o2-g-requires-first-an-exot-2004-marks-4-czslorwmhsejucet.htm","content":"The formation of the oxide ion O<sup>2-</sup>(g) requires first an exothermic and then an endothermic\nstep as shown below <br><br>\nO<sub>(g)</sub> + e<sup>-</sup> = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.207ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.927ex\" height=\"3.071ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 1735.5 1357.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(796,411.6) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(796,-356.7) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(869,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org